TI  - Bacteriophage Therapy for Chronic Mastoiditis.
AB  - To provide the first description of intratympanic bacteriophage therapy for chronic mastoiditis from multidrug-resistant Pseudomonas aeruginosa in the United States. A 47-year-old woman with chronic mastoiditis in the setting of ciliary dysfunction from cystic fibrosis and immunosuppression from lung transplantation. Ten concurrent parenteral and intratympanic doses of two custom phages targeting P. aeruginosa followed by IV antibiotic therapy. Resolution of infection confirmed by symptomatology, cultures, and imaging. At 5 months after phage treatment, the patient reported resolution of otorrhea, headaches, and hearing impairment. Subsequent cultures showed no growth. Bacteriophages can enhance antibiotic activity in cases of drug-resistant chronic mastoiditis.
