TI  - Genome sequences of two phages active against cystic fibrosis isolates of Pseudomonas aeruginosa.
AB  - We describe the genomes of two Pseudomonas aeruginosa phages of the genus Bruynoghevirus, WRAIR_EPa83 and WRAIR_EPa87. They consist of 45,622 and 45,077 bp, with 52.52% and 52.11% guanine-cytosine content, contain 81 and 80 coding sequences, two and three tRNA genes, and direct terminal repeats of 183 and 184 bp, respectively.
